# EAS Build only — files here are excluded from the tarball uploaded to
# EAS, but stay in the repo. This is independent of .gitignore.
# Without this file EAS uploaded ~248 MB and hit EPIPE pipe failures
# repeatedly on Google Cloud Storage. dist/ alone is ~308 MB.

# Web export output — EAS Build is mobile-only, doesn't need it.
dist/

# Git history — EAS pulls a clean clone from your remote already.
.git/

# Local docs the build doesn't compile.
docs/

# Local-only debug scripts.
*.log
.DS_Store

# Vercel artifacts.
.vercel/

# Test outputs.
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# Editor stuff.
.vscode/
.idea/

# 2026-05-25 — Major bloat trim. Previous tarball was 752MB and EPIPE'd
# on Google Cloud Storage twice in a row. Excluding these brings the
# upload to ~100MB cleanly. All four are regenerated server-side by
# `expo prebuild` or `npm install` during the build.
node_modules/
ios/
android/
.claude/

# 2026-09-21 — .easignore SUPERSEDES .gitignore entirely ("if .easignore exists, .gitignore files
# are not used" — eas-cli/build/vcs/local.js). So every gitignored secret was being uploaded to the
# EAS builder, including .env.local — whose EXPO_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the production
# bundle at export.
#
# That matters because of one variable. Any non-empty EXPO_PUBLIC_OWNER_EMAIL makes the BUNDLE an
# owner bundle: Owner Tools on every player's Settings screen and grantLifetime for everyone,
# bypassing billing. scripts/ota-owner-guard.mjs exists to stop exactly that — and it is wired into
# `ota:production` only, never into ios:ship or android:build:production. The build door was
# unguarded, and .env.local is one uncommented line away from shipping owner mode to the App Store.
#
# It is all comments today (verified: `grep -c '^[^#]' .env.local` → 0), so no build shipped this.
# Keeping .env.example, which carries no values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Signing material and credentials have no business on a builder that uses remote credentials.
credentials.json
*.jks
